      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "means allurement or distraction; one commentary explains it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "also as आदर. पर्यस्त. lit. tossed about; hence distracted. अल्पत्वं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "दधति—the man engaged in the pursuit of wordly objects finds",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "time too short to achieve all his ends. वासराणां the gen. by अधीग-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "र्थदयेषां कर्मणि’ Pán II. 3. 52. ध्यानच्छेदे—ध्यान is defined by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "Patanjali as ‘तत्र प्रत्ययैकतानता ( sameness of perception; see",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "com. sl. 99 ). ध्यानम्’—(1) at the end of my contemplation; (2)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "during the interval between two समाधि s. The idea is this—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "after I shall have broken my समाधि, I shall smile at the life of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "misery led by worldly people. May the time come when I shall",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "be free from desire and renouncing the world enjoy the happi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "ness of समाधि.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 30. संतोष०—संतोषेण निरन्तरं always or greatly, highly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "प्रमुदिताः delighted. Mr. Telang reads संतोषसुखप्रमोदमुदिताः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "but we do not see the propriety of प्रमोद and मुदित which mean",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the same thing. भिन्नाः—interrupted, unaltered; they enjoy",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "unmixed felicity ( not affected by the report about the treasures",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "of Meru ). The joys of ordinary men are often interrupted by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "misfortunes, the thwarting of their desires &c. हता—mark the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "contrast. The happiness of the one never comes to an end; the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "thirst of the other never ends and makes him perpetuall misera-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "ble. इत्थं &c —The sentence ends with मेरुः; supply सः or एत-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "द्विधेः कृत्यं as nom. to रोचते. This indicates Vairágya, and so the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "sl. is in its proper place here. The idea seems to be this—A sane",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "person never does any thing without some motive. But it is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "difficult to see what the motive of Brahmà was in creating",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "Meru. Those who are self-contented have nothing to do with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "it. If the object be to gratify the lust for money of avaricious",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "persons, Meru, with its unending treasures, can never fulfil it.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "“ S'árngadhara p. 20 ascribes this to Vidyápati. ” Mr. Telang.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 31. अदैन्य–in which there is no self-abasement; in which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "one has not the misery of undergoing humiliation, or making",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "abject supplication. अप्रतिमुखं-This reading is better than अप्रति-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "हतं as it nearly means the same thing as अवार्य. अप्रतिहत may",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "mean knowing no obstruction, producing every desired effect.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
